_gate_rev_durability":0.06303577474855526,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":56.5,"_gate_fcf_durability":-0.2522746010705619,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":0.005453770391012131,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":55.5,"_gate_fund_growth":0.061054419979237086,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":61.1,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.027723619085638772,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":41.9,"_gate_share_shrink":0.0030973311602950915,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":46.1,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.004188351893021163,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":93.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.04928,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":32.9,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Standard Motor Products, Inc. manufactures and distributes replacement automotive parts in the United States, Europe, Canada, Mexico, Poland, and internationally. The company operates through four segments: Vehicle Control, Temperature Control, Nissens Automotive, and Engineered Solutions. It provides ignition, emissions, and fuel delivery systems, such as air injection and induction components, air management valves, regulators and solenoids, exhaust gas recirculation components, fuel injectors and components, fuel valves, ignition coils, connectors and sockets, modules, pumps, relays and fuses, starting and charging system parts, and vapor and purge components. The company also offers electrical switches and actuators; anti-lock brake and vehicle speed sensors, fluid level sensors, and pressure sensors comprising tire pressure monitoring, temperature sensors, advanced driver assistance systems sensors, battery cables, pigtails, and sockets; electrical wire, terminals, connectors, and tools for servicing a vehicle's electrical system; and spark plug, coil on plug boots, and ignition system accessories. In addition, it offers AC system components; other thermal components; and engine cooling, air conditioning, and engine efficiency products. Further, it provides thermal management products, sensors, switches, power distribution, electrification and electronics, injections and fuel delivery, ignition and emissions, and clamping devices for commercial and light vehicles, construction, agriculture, power sports, marine, hydraulics, and lawn and garden sectors. It serves retailers, warehouse distributors, original equipment manufacturers and their suppliers, system integrators, and original equipment service part manufacturers. The company was founded in 1919 and is headquartered in Long Island City, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Eric Philip Sills | CEO, President & Chairman | Age 56 | Compensation: $1.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5K people. Revenue per employee of $314K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 5%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $3K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Standard Motor Products, Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $984M market cap on $1.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +9% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 29%.","The business throws off $19M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.39\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 4.4\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 4.9% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 29% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.2934374295706097},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 44% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","16 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Technical Reactions to SMP Trends in Macro Strategies","source"